59 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 29 0 R
/E (The macro backdrop remained complex in June. Global real GDP growth is now forecast at 2.2% for 2026, with the eurozone facing near-stagnant growth of 0.2%, while global consumer price inflation is expected to hold at 4.1% \(S&P Global Economic Outlook, June 2026\). Monetary policy divergence has become more pronounced, with the ECB raising rates by 25 basis points in June while the Fed remains on hold and emerging market central banks increasingly split between hiking and easing. In this environment, short-duration, non-bank credit strategies continue to offer a compelling alternative to rate-sensitive public market exposures. The Fund's portfolio continues to grow and remains well balanced, with exposures diversified across jurisdictions, asset classes, and originator partners. This diversification, combined with the self-liquidating nature of the underlying assets and an average duration of 90-120 days, ensures resilience across varying rate and macro environments. Fundamentals remain solid and the pipeline active heading into the second half of 2026.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [27]
>>
